11
00:56:26,086 --> 00:56:32,086
Saw X is a 2023 American horror film directed and edited by Kevin
Greutert, and written by Peter Goldfinger and Josh Stolberg.

12
01:01:33,913 --> 01:01:39,913
It is the tenth installment in the Saw film series, following Spiral (2021) and stars Tobin Bell and Shawnee Smith, who reprise
their roles from the previous films, alongside Synnøve Macody Lund, Steven Brand, Renata Vaca, and Michael Beach.

13
01:06:41,739 --> 01:06:47,739
Set between the events of Saw (2004) and Saw II (2005), the film sees John Kramer (Bell)
travelling to Mexico in hopes that an experimental procedure may cure his terminal cancer.

14
01:11:49,565 --> 01:11:55,565
John later discovers that the operation is a scam, prompting him to kidnap those responsible and subject them to
his trademark death traps as retribution, with Amanda Young (Smith) acting as his accomplice.

15
01:16:57,391 --> 01:17:03,391
A tenth installment was reported to be in development with Twisted Pictures in April 2021, when Stolberg and Goldfinger,
writers for the previous two entries of the series, announced that they had completed the script in December 2021.

16
01:22:05,217 --> 01:22:11,217
Greutert, who had directed two other installments of the series and
edited six, was also confirmed as the film's director.

17
01:27:13,043 --> 01:27:19,043
Filming took place between October 2022 and February 2023 in Mexico City.

18
01:32:20,869 --> 01:32:26,869
Saw X was theatrically released by Lionsgate Films on September 29, 2023.

19
01:37:28,695 --> 01:37:34,695
It grossed $125 million worldwide and received generally positive
reviews from critics, making it the best-reviewed Saw film.

20
01:42:36,521 --> 01:42:42,521
Following a tumultuous pre-production regarding a follow-up to Saw X, Blumhouse Productions bought out Twisted Pictures' stake in the franchise in
June 2025, with Lionsgate retaining substantial ownership, making this film the last Saw film to be produced by Twisted Pictures.

21
01:47:44,347 --> 01:47:50,347
The film explores themes of mexico, mexico city, mexico, sadism, riddle, gore.

22
01:52:52,173 --> 01:52:58,173
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
